ter the divorce  Johnny Depp's representant released a  statement to tell people that the actor  will not respond to any of the salacious  false stories gossip misinformation and  lies about his personal life his  daughters and his exes Vanessa Paradis  and loriann Allison also defended him in  the  as the actor had never been violent with  them amber was accused of doing this for  the money and this is why she retracted  her request for temporary spousal  support as she thought that it was a  standard operating procedure in a  divorce case but the situation got worse  for the actress when she appeared to be  manic and irrational during her  deposition according to the actor's  lawyer no matter what the divorce case  was finally settled and the restraining  order against Johnny Depp was withdrawn  the couple said in a joint statement  that their relationship was intensely  passionate and at times volatile but  always bound by love neither party has  made false accusations for financial  gains and to prove it the actress said  that she would give the money that she  earned from the divorce to charity no  one knows if he was guilty or not the  two actors simply decided to make an  agreement and Amber Heard has decided to  move on to something else no one is sure  of anything and only the two actors know  what really happened the controversy  during the first movie Johnny Depp had  already been working on fantastic beasts  and where to find them before he was  part of this tragic controversy this is  why we understand why it was hard to  replace this actor but didn't stop some  fans from criticizing this choice  however everyone who worked on the first  fantastic beasts movie defended the  actor JK Rowling said that she was  delighted to see Johnny Depp play  Gelbart Grindelwald as he's done  incredible things with that character  director David Yates also said that fans  had to trust them and see what he does  in the movie you won't see very much in  this movie because he appears in it very  fleetingly he appears much more in the  second movie what you have to remember  about Johnny is that extraordinary  talent and that talent never goes away  Hollywood is such a fickle place people  go up and go down Yeats also added when  talking about death he's a huge potter  fan he loves the world he's beyond  excited about working on this material  in fact he didn't even want to see a  script he just said I'm in David Heyman  the executive producer also added that  here's the thing misogyny abuse  maltreatment of people is unacceptable  but none of us know what happened in  that room this is why he thinks that he  would be unfair for anyone to be the  judge and the jury what the director had  to say Harry Potter fans forgive the  team for letting Johnny Depp be part of  the first fantastic beasts movie but  then many of them were shocked to see  he was still going to be part of  fantastic beasts the crimes of  Grindelwald as he hasn't been replaced  this is why David Yates had to open up  about this once again he told  Entertainment Weekly honestly there's an  issue at the moment where there's a lot  of people being accused of things  they're being accused by multiple  victims and it's compelling and  frightening with Johnny it seems to me  there was one person who took a pop at  him and claimed something he then talked  about the man he sees every day who is  full of decency and kindness and that's  all he sees he said that whatever  accusation was out there it doesn't  tally with the kind of human being that  he has been working with and he's not  the only one as some of the women in  depths life have said the same thing  that's not the human being we know  usually there are multiple accusers over  many years that need to be examined but  that's not the case for the actor he is  not in this category in any shape or  form this is why director David Yates  simply concluded that it's a dead issue  what JK Rowling thinks the author and  scr